/-
# Infomaterial — the relational-generative mathematics library

A **dependency-free** Lean 4 library (no Mathlib; Lean core only) that is the
inductive derivation tree of `561-group/content/`. Each module is generated by the
one before it — read the import spine top-to-bottom and it is a proof.

The rule the whole library obeys: **past `Mark` and `Articulating` there is no free
data.** Those two modules admit the only primitives — the atomic marks and the
articulating recursion. Every module below them *derives* its content; none
introduces an `axiom`, `opaque`, `constant`, or `sorry`.

## The spine so far

* `Infomaterial.Mark`             — the arbitrary atomic primitive; two kinds by position.
* `Infomaterial.Utterance`        — the ordered pair (token, claim); articulating's domain.
* `Infomaterial.Articulating`     — the base morphism; recursive `[utterance, articulating]`.
* `Infomaterial.Articulating.Cell` — articulating's codomain; the derived four-cell partition.
* `Infomaterial.Predicating`      — the morphism out of the potential cell; the predication
                               category and its object φ = (s, p, o). Category theory.
* `Infomaterial.Positing`         — admits value: the FOUR bilattice of charges (= the four
                               phases met as value), the valuation, the ⊥ₖ seed.
* `Infomaterial.Settling`         — the closure ◇∘□ to its fixed point; **generates order**:
                               `≤ₖ` proven a partial order, `∨ₖ`/`∧ₖ` its lub/glb,
                               Knaster–Tarski least fixed point.
* `Infomaterial.Hyperdoctrine`    — quantifier adjoints over reindexing; the converse
                               adjoint system `∃ ⊣ f* ⊣ ∀`, Frobenius, Beck–Chevalley.
* `Infomaterial.Quantifying`      — the fiber quantifier adjoints `∃_f ⊣ f* ⊣ ∀_f` for any
                               finite fibration (covers the projection generators).
* `Infomaterial.TruthOrder`       — the bilattice's **second** order `≤ₜ` as a bounded
                               lattice + truth-order closure; negation is the duality.
* `Infomaterial.ClosureOrdinal`   — settling iterated to its fixed point; the closure
                               ordinal `κ ≤ 3` — the **strict-finite regime**.
* `Infomaterial.Sheaf`            — settling's fixed point as a sheaf `{base, section}`;
                               **H¹ = 0** (CRDT/CALM convergence) + sheaf separation.
* `Infomaterial.Four`             — the capstone: the recurring FOUR is one object (phases =
                               charges = generators); the **Klein-four symmetry** `⟨~,−⟩`.
* `Infomaterial.Positing.Bigraded`  — the first math structure *below* settling: two commuting
                               **nuclei** → the **nuclear quartet** (FOUR as sub-algebras).
* `Infomaterial.Equality`         — the **second adjoint system** `∃^t⊣f*⊣∀^t` (truth order);
                               classical & paraconsistent **equality derived**, not posited.
* `Infomaterial.Closure.Monad`     — the closure-2-monad's KZ/lax-idempotence reduction
                               (`kz_iff_strict`, no periodic orbits, `F_U=Cl∨ₖu` settles).
* `Infomaterial.BigradedCohomology` — the aperiodic-regime **trichotomy** (consistent /
                               paraconsistent / mixed) + the internal **ℤ/2 gauge** (`~`).
-/
